          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q U E S T I O N S"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.137,
            0.666,
            0.154
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. How is the process of pollination different from fertilisation?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.156,
            0.699,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. What is the role of the seminal vesicles and the prostate gland?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.174,
            0.654,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. What are the changes seen in girls at the time of puberty?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.192,
            0.708,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. How does the embryo get nourishment inside the mother’s body?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.211,
            0.749,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. If a woman is using a copper -T, will it help in protecting her from sexually transmitted diseases?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.776,
            0.137,
            0.856,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.776,
                0.137,
                0.856,
                0.235
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.278,
            0.514,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What you have learnt"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.328,
            0.866,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reproduction, unlike other life processes, is not essential to maintain the life of an individual organism.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.364,
            0.864,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reproduction involves creation of a DNA copy and additional cellular apparatus by the cell involved in the process.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.399,
            0.864,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Various organisms use different modes of reproduction depending on their body design.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.436,
            0.864,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In fission, many bacteria and protozoa simply divide into two or more daughter cells.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.472,
            0.864,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Organisms such as hydra can regenerate if they are broken into pieces. They can also give out buds which mature into new individuals.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.508,
            0.864,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Roots, stems and leaves of some plants develop into new plants through vegetative propagation.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.544,
            0.863,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These are examples of asexual reproduction where new generations are created from a single individual.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.579,
            0.863,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sexual reproduction involves two individuals for the creation of a new individual.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.6,
            0.864,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "DNA copying mechanisms creates variations which are useful for ensuring the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "survival of the species. Modes of sexual reproduction allow for greater variation to be generated.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.651,
            0.864,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reproduction in flowering plants involves transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma which is referred to as pollination. This is followed by fertilisation.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.687,
            0.864,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Changes in the body at puberty, such as increase in breast size in girls and new facial hair growth in boys, are signs of sexual maturation.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.723,
            0.864,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The male reproductive system in human beings consists of testes which produce sperms, vas deferens, seminal vesicles, prostate gland, urethra and penis.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.759,
            0.864,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The female reproductive system in human beings consists of ovaries, fallopian tubes, uterus and vagina.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.794,
            0.864,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sexual reproduction in human beings involves the introduction of sperm in the vagina of the female. Fertilisation occurs in the fallopian tube.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.83,
            0.864,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Contraception to avoid pregnancy can be achieved by the use of condoms, oral "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pills, copper-T and other methods.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
